From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Sat, 22 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: add the fold primitives and fold the core range loops
 for n > 2

F0, primitives: field::fold_player and field::unfold_player (identity with 2
duelists), chain::bound_opp, and a scope stack in the interpreter (P, bound
pointer, yieldable, probe, touched) with push, pop and read helpers. Nothing
pushes a scope yet. The Lua entry points do that in the next task.

F2, core ranges: one helper, field::build_range_list, splits a two sided
query into (duelist, locations) entries by location class. Field class
(zones, Graveyard, banished, overlay, counters): self is the team of P,
oppo is every living opponent. Individual class (hand, Deck, Extra Deck):
self is P, oppo is the bound opponent of the scope, or every living
opponent when nothing is bound (the scope is marked touched). Tag partners
are never oppo. Eliminated duelists are skipped.

Changed sites: 4 range loops (filter_affected_cards, filter_inrange_cards,
filter_matching_card, filter_field_card), 3 release lists (get_release_list,
get_summon_release_list, ritual material), 2 material lists (ritual xyz and
fusion, partner cards allowed), 2 overlay loops, get_field_counter, 2 unique
card lists, 2 player hint loops in add_effect and remove_effect, and in
effect.cpp is_target, is_target_player and RESET_OPPO_TURN.

With 2 duelists every site builds the same (self, oppo) pair that the stock
loop visited, or keeps the stock text behind n_duelists == 2. So no message,
Lua call or result changes. Sites left for other tasks are in
unchanged-sites.md.

